## Model card
- **Name:** GLM-5.3-FlashX
- **Short description:** Verified faster paid Flash-family endpoint, not an independently verified quality-equivalent rerun of Flash.
- **Provider / access:** Z.AI Chat Completion API and OpenRouter `z-ai/glm-5.3-flashx`; primary docs say not yet on GLM Coding Plan [S1,S3].
- **Release / knowledge:** Exact date/cutoff not verified.
- **IDs:** `glm-5.3-flashx`; no verified Free ID.
- **Context window:** Combined primary Flash/FlashX page specifies1M/128K output [S1].
- **Modalities:** Combined docs specify video/image/text/file input, text output; thinking enabled only, tool calls, structured output, streaming [S1].
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-16):** $0.37 input/$0.075 cache/$1.25 output per million; cache storage temporarily free, search$0.01/use [S2].
- **Architecture:** Family docs describe Flash320B/18B hybrid sparse/linear model; exact FlashX weight/quantization identity not independently confirmed [S1].

### Raw benchmarks found
Agent / tool use, reasoning / knowledge, coding, long-context retrieval and multimodal quality: **no verified exact-FlashX public numeric quality score found** in inspected material. TB2.1, Tau3, GDPval-AA, HLE, GPQA, CritPt, SWE, DeepSWE, Vibe and MMMU results on the combined page are explicitly Flash-labelled and are not transferred.

Primary advertises FlashX **200 tokens/s** [S1], without inspected workload/methodology. This is a serving-speed claim, not sufficient evidence to calculate the five quality dimensions. Distinct route/rate verification establishes existence, not equivalent accuracy.

### Evidence comparison and research trail
Three fresh Google searches: `"GLM-5.3-FlashX" official model`, `"GLM-5.3-FlashX" independent benchmark`, `"GLM-5.3-FlashX" pricing review limitations`; all interstitials. Direct exact guessed AA, BenchLM and Vals profiles returned404; this does not prove complete absence under other names. Read primary combined model docs, exact pricing and OpenRouter route docs. Combined headings/capabilities are useful specifications, but the numeric quality paragraphs explicitly say Flash. No explicit inspected statement that FlashX uses identical weights/quality warrants promoting sibling scores into exact-route evidence.

